slug:'carlsbad',name:'Carlsbad',title:'Carlsbad Remodeling: Room Plans & Permit Preparation',
intro:'A Carlsbad remodel can start with a kitchen layout and quickly become a project involving windows, lighting and outdoor access. Separate those decisions early: the City specifically lists kitchen and bathroom remodels, replacement windows and new or relocated lighting among work that generally needs a building permit.',
sections:[
['Price the kitchen and the exterior opening separately','If the goal is a kitchen that opens toward the yard, compare two drawings: one retaining the existing opening and one enlarging it. The second option can involve a beam, revised weather protection and exterior repairs. Keeping those costs visible makes it easier to decide whether the opening matters more than a cabinet or appliance upgrade.'],
['Ask Carlsbad for the right application route','Carlsbad offers select permits online; its Building Permits page explains alternatives for other work. Residential applications use the City’s residential forms. Before submission, identify whether the project is a room remodel, addition or combination of scopes. For a preliminary permit-fee estimate, the City provides form B-40; that estimate is separate from construction pricing.',0],
['Resolve parcel questions before exterior design','Carlsbad’s Planning Division handles zoning and coastal-program questions. Ask staff to check the actual parcel before committing to a new deck, addition or change to the building envelope. If your property has an association, obtain its architectural requirements separately. Neither a neighborhood name nor HOA approval establishes which City approvals apply.',1]
],checklist:['Existing and proposed kitchen plans, including any changed exterior opening','Window schedule showing replacements versus resized openings','Property address and parcel number for Planning’s location check','Separate allowances for interior work and exterior restoration'],
question:'Will a permit-fee estimate tell me the total remodel cost?',answer:'No. Carlsbad’s fee-estimate process concerns City charges. Ask ADELIE to price demolition, trades, fixtures and finishes separately, then combine the confirmed fees and owner purchases into the total budget.',
links:[['Kitchen scope and budgeting','kitchen-remodel-cost-san-diego.html'],['Planning a home addition','home-additions.html']],
