slug:'solana-beach',name:'Solana Beach',title:'Solana Beach Remodeling: Height, Views & Lot Review',
intro:'A Solana Beach project that changes building height deserves an early Planning conversation. The City’s planning-permit guidance identifies a Structure Development Permit and View Assessment process for new construction exceeding 16 feet above pre-existing grade. Have staff determine how the rule applies to your proposed work.',
sections:[
['Test the roof profile before developing the room','For an upper-level addition or taller living space, start with a measured section through the house and lot. An interior ceiling height is only one part of the exterior height calculation. Show the roof profile, existing grade and nearby relationships so Planning can identify the relevant review.',0],
['Separate Planning approval from building review','Solana Beach lists Development Review Permits and Structure Development Permits among its discretionary processes. Building Services separately reviews construction documents and determines permit needs based on scope and location. A larger renovation should have an approval sequence before it has a firm demolition date.',1,2],
['Keep a lower-impact option on the table','If the objective is better daylight or storage, compare a revised interior layout with an addition before choosing the larger scope. A kitchen reconfiguration or carefully placed opening may address the daily problem without the same roof changes. That comparison needs drawings and prices; it should not assume the smaller project is automatically exempt.']
],checklist:['Measured roof and grade information for height questions','A statement of the problem the addition must solve','Existing and proposed exterior views','A comparison between an interior renovation and expanded floor area'],question:'Is view assessment required for every Solana Beach kitchen remodel?',answer:'The City’s cited height rule concerns qualifying new construction. It is not a blanket requirement for every interior kitchen update. Planning should classify the actual proposal, particularly where the roof or exterior dimensions change.',links:[['Kitchen layout planning','kitchen-planning-guide.html'],['Addition feasibility','home-additions.html']],sources:[['Solana Beach Planning Permits','https://cityofsolanabeach.ca.gov/en/government/departments/community-development/planning/planning-permits'],['Solana Beach Planning','https://cityofsolanabeach.ca.gov/en/government/departments/community-development/planning'],['Solana Beach Building Services','https://www.cityofsolanabeach.ca.gov/en/building-services']]
