slug:'oceanside',name:'Oceanside',title:'Oceanside Remodeling: Digital Plans & Coastal Scope',
intro:'Oceanside’s building applications with plans now use electronic submission. Organizing a complete digital package is part of getting the project moving: the City states that plan-review time does not start until required documents have been submitted and fees paid.',
sections:[
['Build one consistent set of drawings','Before uploading, reconcile the floor plan with the electrical, plumbing and cabinet drawings. A sink relocation shown on one sheet but omitted from another can leave the scope unclear. Keep the submitted set and later corrections in one project folder so a supplier does not order from an obsolete drawing.',0],
['Do not treat a coastal remodel as an interior-only label','A published Oceanside coastal-permit record includes a residential remodel with exterior materials, relocated windows, dormers and balcony repairs. It is an example of a City approval, not an ADELIE project or a rule for every coastal home. If your scope changes the exterior in the coastal zone, ask Planning to classify it before promising a simple interior-remodel schedule.',1],
['Coordinate utility replacement with the room work','Oceanside lists several eligible equipment and utility permits through eTRAKiT, including residential re-pipes and like-for-like equipment replacement. When those tasks accompany a larger remodel, ask which application route applies to the combined scope. Plan shutoffs and wall repairs together to avoid finishing a room before related utility work is complete.',0]
],checklist:['A complete PDF plan set with matching revision dates','A separate description of windows, balconies and exterior changes','Permit invoices and confirmation of document acceptance','A shutoff and restoration plan for any re-pipe or equipment change'],question:'Does uploading an application mean plan review has started?',answer:'Not necessarily. Oceanside’s instructions connect the start of review to required documents and payment. Confirm acceptance and outstanding items before making schedule commitments.',links:[['Estimate inclusions','contractor-estimate-comparison-guide.html'],['Plumbing remodeling','plumbing-remodeling.html']],sources:[['Oceanside Building Permits','https://www.ci.oceanside.ca.us/residents/building-permits'],['State CEQAnet: Oceanside coastal remodel record','https://ceqanet.lci.ca.gov/2025040043']]
