slug:'san-marcos',name:'San Marcos',title:'San Marcos Remodeling: Plans, Portals & Utility Choices',
intro:'San Marcos has moved new building-permit applications from its older eTRAKiT system to a newer portal. Use the current Building Division page to start an application; an old bookmarked search screen may still show records without being the right place to submit new work.',
sections:[
['Start from the current City instructions','The legacy eTRAKiT notice points applicants to the replacement portal. San Marcos’s current Building Division page also organizes guidance for home remodeling, inspections, contractors and permit-ready ADUs. Choose the route for the work you are actually proposing before assembling forms from an older project.',0,1],
['Decide on appliances before the electrical scope','For a kitchen renovation that changes cooking equipment, identify the appliance models and electrical requirements before cabinet fabrication. If the household also wants an EV charger or other equipment, include it in the load discussion. San Marcos publishes separate EV and solar guidance; those improvements should be coordinated with the remodel instead of discovered after the panel work is priced.',1],
['Compare an ADU with a room addition by intended use','San Marcos provides permit-ready ADU resources, but an ADU and a larger primary home solve different problems. Write down whether you need independent living, a guest room or more shared family space. Then compare site access, utilities and layout. A standard plan can inform the discussion without establishing that it fits a particular lot.']
],checklist:['Current City application link and the project contact responsible for submissions','Appliance specifications and proposed additional electrical loads','A clear distinction between independent living and added space in the main home','Site dimensions for any ADU-plan comparison'],question:'Can I use the old San Marcos eTRAKiT link to file a new remodel?',answer:'The old portal directs new building applications to its replacement. Follow the current Building Division link so your application reaches the active system.',links:[['Kitchen appliance and layout planning','kitchen-planning-guide.html'],['ADU construction','adu-construction.html']],sources:[['San Marcos legacy portal migration notice','https://etrakit9.san-marcos.net/etrakit/'],['San Marcos Building Division','https://www.sanmarcosca.gov/Business-Services/Building-Division']]
