slug:'escondido',name:'Escondido',title:'Escondido Remodeling: Historic Homes & Modern Interiors',
intro:'In Escondido, check historic status before treating windows, a porch or exterior paint as routine selections. The City asks owners of properties on its historic inventories or registers, and owners within Old Escondido, to contact Planning before beginning home improvements.',
sections:[
['Keep the preservation question separate from the kitchen layout','A new kitchen can be planned around the home’s existing character, but the design may also propose replacement windows or changes to a porch. List those exterior changes individually. Escondido’s preservation guidance identifies windows, additions, roofing and exterior paint among work that may need additional review.',0],
['Bring any Mills Act agreement into the discussion','If the property has an existing Mills Act contract, the City advises reviewing its stipulations with Planning. Give the designer those documents before specifying exterior replacements. Do not assume that a product sold as historically styled meets the requirements attached to the property.',0],
['Submit the remodel through the designated portal','Escondido lists residential alterations/remodels and custom ADUs among applications that must use its portal, and accepts construction plans electronically. Build the submission around one defined scope. Separate work retained for character from work replaced for function so the contractor’s price reflects both decisions.',1]
],checklist:['Address check against Old Escondido and the City’s historic lists','Any Mills Act contract or prior preservation decision','Photographs of windows, porch details and exterior materials','A room plan distinguishing repairs, retained features and replacements'],question:'Is every older Escondido home a designated historic resource?',answer:'Age alone does not establish designation. The City identifies inventories, registers and the Old Escondido neighborhood as reasons to consult Planning. Ask about the specific property and proposed work.',links:[['Material selection','material-selection-guide.html'],['Whole-home renovation planning','whole-home-remodel-guide.html']],sources:[['Escondido Historic Preservation','https://www.escondido.gov/367/Historic-Preservation'],['Escondido Building Division','https://www.escondido.gov/215/Building']]
