slug:'chula-vista',name:'Chula Vista',title:'Chula Vista Remodeling: Additions & Complete Budgets',
intro:'Chula Vista separates residential addition/remodel applications from accessory projects and new construction. That distinction matters when a wish list combines an interior kitchen, a patio cover and new living space: the paperwork and supporting requirements may differ even when one contractor coordinates the work.',
sections:[
['Define added living area before comparing prices','Chula Vista’s permit guidance identifies school-fee compliance for projects adding habitable square footage. It also identifies water and sewer service verification for new buildings. Ask which items apply to your proposal and include them in the owner’s project budget rather than assuming the construction subtotal covers them.',0],
['Choose the forms that describe the complete scope','The City publishes a residential addition/remodel application alongside a separate residential accessory application for patio covers, pools and walls. If the project includes both, mark each component on a site plan and ask staff how to submit them. This prevents an outdoor improvement from disappearing between the design brief and the permit package.',1],
['Use review goals as planning inputs','Chula Vista publishes plan-check goals and explains that completeness affects processing. A first review is not the same as permit issuance: corrections, outside approvals and unpaid fees can remain. Schedule cabinet fabrication around a stable layout and verified milestones, rather than treating a published review goal as a guaranteed construction start.',0]
],checklist:['Existing versus added habitable area','A site plan that includes accessory structures as well as the house','A budget line for applicable agency and school fees','Responsibility for each correction and outside-agency item'],question:'Can the kitchen and patio be priced as a single project?',answer:'Yes, a coordinated proposal can cover both. It should still separate their scope and permit responsibilities so you can see what each improvement costs and what approvals remain.',links:[['Complete remodel budgets','home-remodeling-cost-san-diego.html'],['Additions','home-additions.html']],sources:[['Chula Vista application and review guidance','https://www.chulavistaca.gov/departments/development-services/permit-information/permit-process/project-submittal-process/application-general-information'],['Chula Vista forms and specifications','https://www.chulavistaca.gov/departments/development-services/resources/dsdformsspecifications']]
