slug:'coronado',name:'Coronado',title:'Coronado Remodeling: Preserve Character, Improve Function',
intro:'Coronado’s historic-review rules can affect a remodel well before finishes are selected. The City requires a Historic Resource Alteration Permit review for exterior modifications to designated resources. It also describes a separate significance-review trigger for certain work on structures at least 75 years old, with inventory-related exceptions.',
sections:[
['Confirm status before removing original features','Ask Coronado’s preservation staff about the property’s designation and inventory status when demolition or removal of street-visible original features is proposed. The City’s guidance describes the conditions and exceptions; age alone is not a complete permit determination. Keep photographs and records of features you may want to alter.',0],
['Design the interior around what should remain','A practical kitchen brief can distinguish inconvenient circulation from features worth retaining. Locate cabinets, appliances and lighting around that brief before proposing enlarged windows or an altered front elevation. If exterior work is necessary, include it in the preservation discussion at the beginning.'],
['Check the limits of simple replacement permits','Coronado’s Building Services page lists specific replacement scopes available through simpler routes, including like-for-like reroofing for non-historic properties. That qualification matters: a replacement label does not automatically establish eligibility when a property has historic status. Submit the actual scope and property information together.',1]
],checklist:['Historic designation and inventory information','Photographs of original street-visible elements','Any recorded preservation agreement','Interior alternatives that retain important exterior features'],question:'Is an older house automatically subject to the same review as a designated resource?',answer:'No. Coronado describes different processes for designated resources and potential historic significance. Ask staff which category applies to the property and work, including any inventory exceptions.',links:[['Kitchen planning','kitchen-planning-guide.html'],['Choosing compatible materials','material-selection-guide.html']],sources:[['Coronado Historic Preservation','https://www.coronado.ca.us/256/Historic-Preservation'],['Coronado Building Services','https://www.coronado.ca.us/247/Building-Services']]
