slug:'imperial-beach',name:'Imperial Beach',title:'Imperial Beach Remodeling: Flood & Coastal Checks',
intro:'For an Imperial Beach home, establish whether the parcel is in a Special Flood Hazard Area before settling a major renovation budget. The City’s substantial-improvement guidance describes additional documentation and possible floodplain requirements for qualifying work on existing buildings. This is a parcel-specific check, not a statement that every home in the city is affected.',
sections:[
['Ask about the scope before splitting it into phases','For affected properties, the City’s notice calls for a detailed work description and cost information, with building-value documentation addressed in the review. Bring the intended renovation to the Building Official early. Do not assume that calling work a repair or dividing it into separate contracts resolves the floodplain question.',0],
['Treat coastal and flood reviews as different checks','Imperial Beach’s FAQ says coastal-zone development needs a coastal permit unless exempt under its municipal code. Coastal location and flood designation are different issues. Ask Planning about the coastal process and Building about the flood-related requirements; keep both answers with the project records.',1],
['Plan the construction package around confirmed requirements','Imperial Beach uses its Citizen Self-Service portal for building applications, plan check and payment. Once the review path is known, align the submitted scope with the contractor’s proposal. For exterior work, specify the window, flashing and finish assemblies in enough detail to compare bids and maintenance needs.',2]
],checklist:['Parcel flood-area determination and any elevation records','Full proposed scope and construction-cost estimate','Coastal permit or exemption determination','Existing-condition photos before repair or demolition'],question:'Does being near the beach mean my remodel must be elevated?',answer:'No automatic conclusion follows from proximity alone. The parcel’s flood designation, building information and proposed work determine which questions the City must evaluate. Obtain that determination before final design.',links:[['Whole-home budgeting','home-remodeling-cost-san-diego.html'],['Remodel versus rebuild','remodel-or-rebuild.html']],sources:[['Imperial Beach substantial-improvement notice','https://www.imperialbeachca.gov/DocumentCenter/View/270/Substantial-Improvement-Notice-Final-PDF'],['Imperial Beach Planning FAQ','https://www.imperialbeachca.gov/m/faq?cat=23'],['Imperial Beach Building Division','https://www.imperialbeachca.gov/225/Building-Division']]
